SU(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    su - run a shell as another account

SYNOPSIS
    su [-lp] [name]

DESCRIPTION
    su is the su of ubase, compiled unmodified from third_party/ubase. It
    runs the shell of the account name, root by default. su is set user
    id root. A caller other than root types the password of the target
    account, which su reads from the terminal without echo, and input
    typed before the prompt appears is discarded. An account whose
    password is locked or empty cannot be entered by others, and a wrong
    password ends su with "su: incorrect password".

    Without options su keeps the environment and sets HOME and SHELL, and
    also USER and LOGNAME unless the target is root. With -p the shell
    named by SHELL in the environment runs instead of the shell of the
    account. With -l su starts a login shell in the home of the account
    with an environment that holds only HOME, SHELL, USER, LOGNAME and
    TERM, as login(1) does.

    su runs no single command. A command is run as another account with
    doas(1) or sudo(1), and a program that has to pass a password through
    a pipe uses sudo -S.

EXAMPLES
    su
    su -l anna

SEE ALSO
    doas(1), sudo(1), login(1), passwd(1), id(1), index(7)
